1-4)/(5-2) = -3/3 = -1 not allowed.\n\nLine through (2,4) and (3,2): slope = (2-4)/(3-2) = -2, allowed. Equation: y-4 = -2 (x-2) => y = -2x + 8. Points: (2,4),(3,2),(4,0) not allowed. So line covers (2,4),(3,2). That's 2 points.\n\nLine through (2,4) and (4,1): slope = (1-4)/(4-2) = -3/2, allowed. Equation: y-4 = -3/2 (x-2) => y = -3/2 x + 7. Points: x=2 => y=4; x=4 => y=1; x=6 => y=-2 not allowed. So line covers (2,4),(4,1). That's 2 points.\n\nLine through (1,2) and (2,1): slope = (1-2)/(2-1) = -1 not allowed.\n\nLine through (1,3) and (2,1): slope = (1-3)/(2-1) = -2, allowed. Equation: y-3 = -2 (x-1) => y = -2x + 5. Points: (1,3),(2,1),(3,-1) not allowed. So line covers (1,3),(2,1). That's 2 points.\n\nLine through (1,4) and (2,1): slope = (1-4)/(2-1) = -3, allowed. Equation: y-4 = -3 (x-1) => y = -3x + 7. Points: (1,4),(2,1),(3,-2) not allowed. So line covers (1,4),(2,1). That's 2 points.\n\nLine through (1,4) and (3,2): slope = (2-4)/(3-1) = -2/2 = -1 not allowed.\n\nLine through (1,2) and (3,2): slope = (2-2)/(3-1) = 0 not allowed.\n\nLine through (1,2) and (5,1): slope = (1-2)/(5-1) = -1/4, allowed. Equation: y-2 = -1/4 (x-1) => y = -x/4 + 9/4. Points: x=1 => y=2; x=5 => y=1; x=9 => y=0 not allowed. So line covers (1,2),(5,1). That's 2 points.\n\nThus many lines cover only 2 points. We need triples. Let's try to find a line covering (1,2),(3,2),(5,2) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,2),(2,4),(3,6) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,4),(2,2),(3,0) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,4),(2,2),(3,0) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,4),(2,2),(3,0) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,4),(2,2),(3,0) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,4),(2,2),(3,0) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,4),(2,2),(3,0) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering (1,4),(2,2),(3,0) not allowed. So maybe we need to use a line covering